# Lauren Tan: Dune, trust, and agent skills

Lauren describes verification as a path from reproducible runs and evidence to stronger methods. She separates correctness from quality: verification checks whether a feature works, while skills can encode senior engineering workflows. [06:45](https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2101938030122868736/vid/avc1/3442x2160/BQlPlAZCEVPDemv1.mp4#t=405) [12:45](https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2101938030122868736/vid/avc1/3442x2160/BQlPlAZCEVPDemv1.mp4#t=765)

Her trust ladder puts codebase changes, static analysis, rules, skills, and style guides in order from more durable to less enforceable. She also describes Dune as a framework designed so the shortcut is the right path. [15:00](https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2101938030122868736/vid/avc1/3442x2160/BQlPlAZCEVPDemv1.mp4#t=900) [19:01](https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2101938030122868736/vid/avc1/3442x2160/BQlPlAZCEVPDemv1.mp4#t=1141)
